    "solution": "Throw the lantern into the western water intake and let the current carry it down, through the one-tile conduit, and up to the high clasp. Once delivery is visible, strike the condenser. That same connected pool now blocks the crossing beam and becomes the solid intake and upper return wall. Climb the intake, jump from the small stone sill onto the dock, hold Down to load it, then release and jump with its rise. Dash onto the broad shelf below the frozen outlet. Dash upward beside the ice and hold Jump to bounce onto the higher outboard rest; a short rising transfer and climb reaches the crown. Reclaim the lantern from its clasp and take the wide, shaded glide across the final beams.",
    "nearestExisting": "F14 Empty Your Hands separates cargo and knight through a one-tile water duct, while F18 The Thawing Track changes ice support to relocate useful shade. This room keeps one connected pool and asks it to do opposing jobs: liquid delivers the lantern, then the frozen outlet becomes the knight’s beam shield and wallbounce face. The dock launch draws on B39’s stored lift, but its useful destination exists only after the earlier cargo route is deliberately closed.",
    "novelty": "The knight manufactures a return structure from the route that transported the object. Freezing first prevents delivery; leaving it liquid removes the dry wall and exposes the approach to a beam. The later object reunion supplies the easy shaded finish, so the hard movement happens before the final reward.",
